{
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "updatedAt": "2026-10-08",
  "note": "How well each option suits a community's size (enums.json communitySize), from -2 (strains badly) to +2 (suits it well); null = size makes no real difference. The rule (2026-10-09): score how the approach behaves at each size as it's normally used, without assuming more people take part in each process as the community grows. Strain counts only when the approach by its nature needs the whole membership (everyone must agree; every member approves each newcomer; a community-wide vote on a dispute), needs people to know each other personally, or makes a few people's work grow with every member or case (one leader deciding everything; a few reviewers reading every application). 'Suits it' = designed for many people (delegation, sampling, standing bodies). Formal structure in a small group is overhead, not failure: at most -1. Used in suggestions (js/recommend.js), where it counts for less than the other signals. Only status \"accepted\" is used. Reviewed in the workbench, bench.html.",
